window.docContents[54].resolve({"/Theorems/#section-the-andr-sfai-erd-s-s-s-theorem":{"contents":"Turán's theorem says that the densest (r + 1)-clique-free graphs are Turán graphs,\nwhile Füredi's stability theorem tells us that graphs that are almost extremal, in\nterms of number of edges, are almost r-colourable.\n\nThe Andrásfai–Erdős–Sós theorem B. Andrásfai, P. Erdős and V. T. Sós, On the connection between chromatic number, maximal clique and minimal degree of a graph, Discrete Math. 8 (1974), no. 3, 205–218. gives a different\ntype of stability result related to the minimum degree: any (r + 1)-clique-free\ngraph with minimum degree greater than (3 * r - 4) * n / (3 * r - 1) must be\nr-colourable. For r = 2 this says that a triangle-free graph with minimum degree\ngreater than 2 * n / 5 is bipartite. The uniform blow-up C[5][t] shows that\n2 * n / 5 cannot be lowered (Exercise 12).\n\nThe 3-uniform blow-up C[5][3]: a non-bipartite triangle-free graph with minimum degree 2 * n / 5\n\n#check colorable_of_cliqueFree_lt_minDegree\n\n\nPut the other way round: a triangle-free graph that contains an odd closed walk, and\nso is not bipartite (isBipartite_iff_forall_walk_even_length), has minimum degree\nat most 2 * n / 5.\n\nexample [Fintype V] [DecidableRel G.Adj] (h3 : G.CliqueFree 3) {u : V}\n    (w : G.Walk u u) (hw : Odd w.length) : δ(G) ≤ 2 * Fintype.card V / 5 := by\n  by_contra! h\n  have hb : G.IsBipartite := colorable_of_cliqueFree_lt_minDegree h3 h\n  exact Nat.not_even_iff_odd.2 hw (isBipartite_iff_forall_walk_even_length.1 hb u w)\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Theorems\u0009Turán's Theorem, Stability and Asymptotics","header":"13.2.5. The Andrásfai–Erdős–Sós Theorem","id":"/Theorems/#section-the-andr-sfai-erd-s-s-s-theorem"}});